These trade-offs are the backbone of experimental design.

Key Relationships: The file highlights critical trade-offs in experimental design:

Stricter thresholds (lower α) typically increase β and reduce power
Larger sample sizes decrease β and increase power
Bigger effect sizes and lower variance both improve power

Bottom Line: These three metrics (α, β, and Power) are interconnected and form the 
foundation for designing rigorous statistical experiments. You must balance Type I 
and Type II error risks based on your research context.
